  "title": "Archive-It mayoral URL adjudication",
  "instructions": "### What to decide\n- Review the named candidate, mayoral contest, claimed URL, collection metadata, and archive evidence.\n- The machine-proposed grade is context only. No claim is accepted until you code it here.\n- If collection metadata identifies the original campaign domain but the claimed URL is an archive-container path, enter the original domain as the corrected URL.\n- Code URL type for the URL you accept (the corrected URL when one is entered).\n\n### Evidence grades\n- A: an election-period capture of the exact URL identifies the candidate, mayoral campaign, and city.\n- B: a contemporaneous official source links the URL and archived content confirms the campaign.\n- C: a source supports the URL, but no qualifying campaign capture exists.\n- D: domain shape, registration data, or current content provides only a lead.\n- Only grades A and B count as strict coverage.\n\n### Scope\n- The task contains every Archive-It candidate-domain claim.\n- The inclusion-reason field identifies proposed strict positives and the deterministic 10% non-strict audit subset.",
